    "['set system radius-server [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa new-model', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco IOS configuration for the given Juniper RADIUS server commands:\\n\\n##\\naaa new-model\\nradius-server host 10.6.55.55 auth-port 1645 acct-port 1646 key 051b1c224d0a324e1d\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS:\\n1. The \"aaa new-model\" enables the AAA security services\\n2. The \"radius-server host\" command combines both authentication and accounting ports in a single command\\n3. The secret key is specified with the \"key\" parameter\\n4. Cisco uses \"auth-port\" instead of just \"port\" for the authentication port', 'trans_template': 'aaa new-model'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'radius-server host 10.6.55.55 auth-port 1645 acct-port 1646 key 051b1c224d0a324e1d', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'radius-server host 10.6.55.55 auth-port 1645 acct-port 1646 key 051b1c224d0a324e1d', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco IOS configuration for the given Juniper RADIUS server commands:\\n\\n##\\naaa new-model\\nradius-server host 10.6.55.55 auth-port 1645 acct-port 1646 key 051b1c224d0a324e1d\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS:\\n1. The \"aaa new-model\" enables the AAA security services\\n2. The \"radius-server host\" command combines both authentication and accounting ports in a single command\\n3. The secret key is specified with the \"key\" parameter\\n4. Cisco uses \"auth-port\" instead of just \"port\" for the authentication port', 'trans_template': 'radius-server host 10.6.55.55 auth-port 1645 acct-port 1646 key 051b1c224d0a324e1d'}]]": 1,
    "['port [parameter2] secret [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper command `set interfaces ge-0/0/1 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.1.1/24` to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1\\n ip address 10.1.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nThe translation notes:\\n1. \"ge-0/0/1\" becomes \"GigabitEthernet0/0/1\" in Cisco\\n2. Cisco doesn\\'t use \"unit\" notation like Juniper\\n3. The subnet mask is converted from CIDR (/24) to dotted decimal (255.255.255.0)\\n4. The family inet specification is implied by the ip address command in Cisco', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip address 10.1.1.1 255.255.255.0', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper command `set interfaces ge-0/0/1 unit 0 family inet address 10.1.1.1/24` to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1\\n ip address 10.1.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nThe translation notes:\\n1. \"ge-0/0/1\" becomes \"GigabitEthernet0/0/1\" in Cisco\\n2. Cisco doesn\\'t use \"unit\" notation like Juniper\\n3. The subnet mask is converted from CIDR (/24) to dotted decimal (255.255.255.0)\\n4. The family inet specification is implied by the ip address command in Cisco', 'trans_template': 'ip address 10.1.1.1 255.255.255.0'}]]": 1,
