    "['family [parameter2] network [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip local pool pool1 10.10.10.3 10.10.10.100 mask 255.255.255.0', 'parent_command': ['ipv6 dhcp pool [parameter1]'], 'root': 'ipv6 dhcp pool [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command:\\n\\n##\\nip local pool pool1 10.10.10.3 10.10.10.100 mask 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Cisco command combines both the network declaration and the range specification into a single command. The \"ip local pool\" creates a DHCP pool named \"pool1\" with the specified range (10.10.10.3-10.10.10.100) and network mask (255.255.255.0 for /24). While not an exact 1:1 translation, this is the functionally equivalent configuration in Cisco IOS for creating a local address assignment pool.', 'trans_template': 'ip local pool pool1 10.10.10.3 10.10.10.100 mask 255.255.255.0'}]]": 1,
