    "['family [parameter2] prefix [parameter3] prefix-length [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv6 local pool pool1 2001:db8:3::/64 64', 'parent_command': ['ipv6 dhcp pool [parameter1]'], 'root': 'ipv6 dhcp pool [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco command for the Juniper IPv6 prefix assignment:\\n\\n##\\nipv6 local pool pool1 2001:db8:3::/64 64\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Cisco uses \"ipv6 local pool\" instead of Juniper\\'s \"access address-assignment pool\"\\n- The pool name \"pool1\" is preserved\\n- The IPv6 prefix \"2001:db8:3::/64\" remains the same\\n- The prefix length \"64\" is specified after the prefix (unlike Juniper where it\\'s a separate parameter)\\n- Cisco doesn\\'t require explicit family specification like Juniper\\'s \"family inet6\"', 'trans_template': 'ipv6 local pool pool1 2001:db8:3::/64 64'}]]": 1,
